@startuml
title CudaWorker restart (per device)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 100
skinparam ranksep 50

' Fatal recovery path. Healthy maintenance is described separately below.
' Sources: runner/cuda_recovery.rs, runner/sync_stage_runner,
' runner/global_ctx.rs, ipc/cuda_process.rs, ipc/pending.rs.

(*) --> "Report fatal CUDA error or IPC transport failure\nfor device d, generation g" as report

note left
NeedsRestart can originate in initialization,
execution, consume, synchronization, or copying.
Actor-owned requests report even if the caller
was cancelled; transport loss is also monitored.
end note

report --> "GlobalCtx::global().get_runner(d)\nrequest_cuda_reset_for_generation(g, cause)\nCudaRecoveryCoordinator::request" as request

request --> if "Gate failed or generation mismatched?" as invalid_report then
    -left->[yes] "Return existing terminal failure;\nignore a retired generation;\nreject a future generation" as reject_report
    --> (*)
else
    -->[no] if "Local mode with NeedsRestart?" as local_fatal then
        -left->[yes] "Fail the device gate; request runner drain\nAbort any healthy maintenance recovery\nGlobalCtx::fail_process" as local_shutdown
        note left
        A poisoned local context requires process relaunch.
        No in-process repair or cudaDeviceReset is attempted.
        Healthy explicit restart is different: it drains the
        device, synchronizes its retained primary context via
        tho_cu_restart, and rebuilds local copy/stream pools.
        It does not reset LibTorch's process-wide state.
        end note
        --> "Close all local CUDA gates\nNotify the application to shut down\nReturn CudaRecoveryFailed" as process_failed
        --> (*)
    else
        -->[IPC] if "Recovery already active for d?" as coalesced then
            -right->[yes] "Join the existing recovery ticket\nReturn ContextReset to admitted work\nUnwind and release activity leases" as joined
            --> (*)
        else
            -->[no] "Close admission on gate d atomically\nOwn its recovery ticket\nSend DrainForRecovery to runner d\nSpawn independent coordinator task" as begin_recovery
        endif
    endif
endif

note right
One gate, runner, actor, and coordinator per device.
Independent GPU and CPU work continues.
Recovery survives cancellation of its reporter.
The admitted reporter returns ContextReset and
unwinds instead of waiting for its own recovery.
Setup errors, panic, abort, or runtime interruption
fail this cycle through the coordinator / RecoveryGuard.
No recovery mutex is held across a drain or rebuild.
end note

begin_recovery --> if "Coordinator setup succeeded?" as setup_ok then
    -->[yes] "Purge queued jobs with ContextReset\nClear OOM reservations and capacity waiters\nResume suspended parents for unwinding\nKeep servicing running-job completions" as drain_runner
else
    -left->[no] "Fail this recovery cycle\nPreserve original cause and recovery error\nKeep gate d closed; wake waiters\nReturn CudaRecoveryFailed" as failed
    note left
    Also reached on errors, panic, coordinator interruption,
    or timeout during drain / retirement / rebuild.
    IPC failure is terminal only for device d.
    No generation is published on failure.
    end note
    --> (*)
endif

drain_runner --> "Wait for runner drain acknowledgment\nand gate d activity count = 0\nDeadline: 30 s" as drain

note right
Leases cover stages, copies, and descendants.
Nested work observing recovery returns ContextReset
so its parents can unwind; active descendants retain
ancestor leases until physical work ends.

Concurrently, the IPC actor reacts to a fatal reply
or transport failure by retiring the old worker.
This resolves pending requests and releases leases
after confirmed process exit, without waiting 30 s.
end note

drain --> if "Drain completed successfully?" as drained then
    -->[yes] "Enter CudaActivityScope::run_reset\nGlobalCtx::reset_cuda_context(d)\nInvalidate cached data only on device d" as reset_hook
else
    -->[no] if "Drain timed out?" as drain_timeout then
        -->[yes] "Send BackendControl::Retire(ticket)\nWait for confirmed worker retirement\nDeadline: 60 s" as retire_fallback
        --> if "Retirement succeeded?" as fallback_ok then
            -->[yes] "Wait for runner drain and idle gate again\nDeadline: 30 s" as drain_again
            --> if "Second drain succeeded?" as drained_again then
                -->[yes] reset_hook
            else
                -left->[error / timeout] failed
            endif
        else
            -left->[error / timeout] failed
        endif
    else
        -left->[error] failed
    endif
endif

reset_hook --> "Send BackendControl::Restart(ticket)\nCheck ticket ownership and idle gate\nRetire old worker if still present" as restart_backend

note right
The entire reset hook has a 60 s deadline,
including cache invalidation and backend restart.
Retire / Restart use a separate priority control
channel, bypassing the bounded work queue.

Retirement, on every path:
1. Close pending-request registration.
2. Stop and join IPC reader/writer tasks.
3. Kill and reap the child (wait deadline: 10 s).
4. Only after exit, free retained shared buffers
   and fail outstanding requests.

A fatal reply can wake its caller earlier, but
its shared storage remains retained until exit.
If exit cannot be confirmed, quarantine storage
and fail waiters; never reuse those allocations.
end note

restart_backend --> if "Authority valid and old worker reaped?" as retired then
    -->[yes] "Spawn new CudaWorker for device d\nAssign identity (d, g + 1)\nSend parent shared-arena descriptor" as spawn_worker
else
    -left->[no / error] failed
endif

spawn_worker --> "Worker obtains a fresh primary context\nInitialize shared mapping and copy/stream pools\nReceive and validate DeviceInfo identity\nReadiness deadline: 30 s" as ready

ready --> if "Replacement ready?" as ready_ok then
    -->[yes] if "Recovery authority still valid?" as authority_ok then
        -->[yes] "Install replacement and acknowledge restart\nCoordinator verifies it still owns the cycle\nPublish generation g + 1 and reopen gate d" as publish
        note right
        Backend acknowledgment precedes gate publication.
        If the replacement dies in that interval, the actor
        waits for publication before reporting its failure.
        Report deduplication and publication share the
        coordinator lock; stale completion cannot reopen a gate.
        end note
    else
        -left->[no] "Retire replacement; do not publish it" as discard_replacement
        --> failed
    endif
else
    -left->[error / timeout] "Kill and reap failed replacement" as failed_startup
    --> failed
endif

publish --> "Wake admission waiters\nReconstruct device stage state on demand\nAccept fresh work in generation g + 1" as resumed

note right
Old tensor / endpoint identities are rejected.
Old cleanup cannot delete replacement state.
Old retry chains return ContextReset: callers must
rebuild generation-bound input/state before retrying.
Other devices retain their generations and caches.
end note

resumed --> (*)

@enduml
